      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Many of these come through the race won by GOOD PHILLY last time. JORUM (9) was one of those. Normally leads but opted out of the speed battle and wound up strongly but was in turn swamped late, finishing runner-up behind GOOD PHILLY. Meets the winner 3kg better and can turn the tables. THE COPS (5) is racing very well and has plenty of speed. Beaten a head this course and distance last time and should give a sight again. MADALSA (2) was fourth in the GOOD PHILLY race winding up late. Better off at the weights and will be running on hard. GOOD PHILLY (3) is hard to knock and will appreciate the good early tempo. Rises 3kg for this but will be winding up strongly. JOTOPELI (8) comes through a Class 1 at Eagle Farm last time. Has a tricky gate but will give a sight.",
